#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:3
msgid "Get a stream as a string, buffer, or array"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:6
msgid "Install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:13
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:48
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:50
msgid ""
"The methods returns a promise that resolves when the `end` event fires on"
" the stream, indicating that there is no more data to be read. The stream"
" is switched to flowing mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:52
msgid "getStream(stream, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:54
msgid "Get the `stream` as a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:56
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:58
msgid "Type: `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:60
msgid "encoding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:62
msgid "Type: `string`<br> Default: `utf8`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:65
msgid ""
"[Encoding](https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html#buffer_buffer) of the "
"incoming stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:67
msgid "maxBuffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:69
msgid "Type: `number`<br> Default: `Infinity`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:72
msgid ""
"Maximum length of the returned string. If it exceeds this value before "
"the stream ends, the promise will be rejected with a "
"`getStream.MaxBufferError` error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:74
msgid "getStream.buffer(stream, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:76
msgid "Get the `stream` as a buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:78
msgid ""
"It honors the `maxBuffer` option as above, but it refers to byte length "
"rather than string length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:80
msgid "getStream.array(stream, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:82
msgid "Get the `stream` as an array of values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:84
msgid ""
"It honors both the `maxBuffer` and `encoding` options. The behavior "
"changes slightly based on the encoding chosen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:86
msgid ""
"When `encoding` is unset, it assumes an [object mode "
"stream](https://nodesource.com/blog/understanding-object-streams/) and "
"collects values emitted from `stream` unmodified. In this case "
"`maxBuffer` refers to the number of items in the array (not the sum of "
"their sizes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:88
msgid ""
"When `encoding` is set to `buffer`, it collects an array of buffers. "
"`maxBuffer` refers to the summed byte lengths of every buffer in the "
"array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:90
msgid ""
"When `encoding` is set to anything else, it collects an array of strings."
" `maxBuffer` refers to the summed character lengths of every string in "
"the array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:93
msgid "Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:95
msgid ""
"If the input stream emits an `error` event, the promise will be rejected "
"with the error. The buffered data will be attached to the `bufferedData` "
"property of the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:109
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:111
msgid ""
"How is this different from [`concat-stream`](https://github.com/maxogden"
"/concat-stream)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/get-stream_readme.md:113
msgid ""
"This module accepts a stream instead of being one and returns a promise "
"instead of using a callback. The API is simpler and it only supports "
"returning a string, buffer, or array. It doesn't have a fragile type "
"inference. You explicitly choose what you want. And it doesn't depend on "
"the huge `readable-stream` package."
msgstr ""

